      "line": 61,
      "observation": "Authentication constructs a fresh ApiTokenAuthenticationToken using the persisted token and current UserDetails for its owner. The token owner and reloaded account must have the same nonblank stable UID; see the 12 November owner-binding record.",
      "limit": "The selected user-attribute list, other authentication mechanisms and complete subject lifecycle are not specified by this mapping.",
      "source_sha256": "be9b3e43ee50dbd23837db71318d460c90ccab7ca0c67589cb2207d701741a97"
    },
    "FIA_USB.1.2": {
      "path": "dhis-2/dhis-web-api/src/main/java/org/hisp/dhis/webapi/security/apikey/ApiTokenAuthManager.java",
      "line": 80,
      "observation": "Before binding a token to a user, validateAndCreateUserDetails checks owner existence and current enabled, credential-expiry, lock, account-expiry and 2FA state. The token owner and reloaded account must have the same nonblank stable UID; see the 12 November owner-binding record.",
      "limit": "This is a partial initial-association rule trace for personal access tokens; selected ST rules and browser/OIDC subjects require separate checks.",
      "source_sha256": "be9b3e43ee50dbd23837db71318d460c90ccab7ca0c67589cb2207d701741a97"
    },
    "FIA_USB.1.3": {
      "path": "dhis-2/dhis-web-api/src/main/java/org/hisp/dhis/webapi/security/apikey/ApiTokenAuthManager.java",
      "line": 61,
      "observation": "The authentication path avoids a process-local snapshot and reloads current owner information on each token request. The token owner and reloaded account must have the same nonblank stable UID; see the 12 November owner-binding record.",
      "limit": "This supports changes between personal access token requests; it does not prove invalidation or propagation for every subject or deployment node.",
      "source_sha256": "be9b3e43ee50dbd23837db71318d460c90ccab7ca0c67589cb2207d701741a97"
    },
    "FTA_SSL.4.1": {
      "path": "dhis-2/dhis-web-api/src/main/java/org/hisp/dhis/webapi/security/config/DhisWebApiWebSecurityConfig.java",
      "line": 436,
      "observation": "The security chain configures logout and removal of session cookies, providing a candidate path for user-initiated session termination.",
      "limit": "A browser logout test must verify server-side invalidation, replay rejection, CSRF handling and all configured session backends. Configuration alone is incomplete evidence.",
