      "source_sha256": "84ec2e1776204de49a88271b2a3a4968219bc0e2a6fc8c7e6adaf16a4797eece",
      "observation": "Login factor acceptance requires a successful durable replay reservation; duplicate keys reject and storage exceptions propagate before authentication returns. Targeted H2 and PostgreSQL tests exercise this failure boundary. Authoritative user-row read/lock failure also prevents acceptance; secret/type mismatch or a deleted user rejects the proof.",
      "limit": "One identified failure case, not the complete selected AFTA failure list or whole-application secure-state proof. Reliable time, restore and broader fault tolerance remain open."
    },
